abel}`, the protected-path defaults above, and the cve, docs, error-codes, lead, engineer, worker, eng-review, security-review and license-review overrides), compares them with `main`, commits them on a new branch `ard-init` cut from `main` through the effect layer and a narrow committer lane, pushes it and opens a PR. It writes nothing to the local working tree or to `main`, and `scan` is committed `100755`. Files that already exist on `main` with different contents are a conflict naming the paths; `--force` proposes overwriting them, and init never deletes anything. It refuses while `ard-init` exists on the remote, whatever its PR's state, so it never force-pushes over or stacks commits on a human's edits: merge or close the PR, delete the branch and rerun. If `main` already has every starter file it prints `nothing to propose`. It syncs the label catalogue first (like `ard labels sync`), so a failure leaves nothing pushed. With `--dry-run` the commit, push and PR are logged to the ledger instead of acting. A missing repo, credentials or `main` branch exits 1 with nothing written, and `ARD_GITHUB_TOKEN` auth is refused outside `--dry-run`. The PR body carries the one step the App cannot do: copy `.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml` and set the repository variable `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` (optionally `ARD_BOT_CHECK_SINCE`). It also says to merge with **Squash and merge** or **Create a merge commit**, never a fast-forward from the command line, which would put the bot's commit on main's first-parent history. **Rebase and merge** is also safe: the scratch-repo run (#85) showed GitHub records the merging human as committer of a rebase-merged commit (the bot stays the author), and the bot-commit check keys on committer, so it does not flag it. The body still names only the two merges above.\n \n **Where `ard serve` reads config (decided, #87).** After each fetch into its own clone (`~/.ard/repos/<owner>/<repo>.git`, see Local-executor details) `ard serve` resolves `origin/main` to a SHA and reads `config.yaml` and the role directories from that commit, not from the working tree. It exports them into a snapshot at `~/.ard/config/<owner>/<repo>/<sha>/`, kept 24 hours after a newer SHA replaces it, because roles run from a host path: a role directory, its `Dockerfile` and the scan worktree must all describe the one commit the tick's jobs use. Editing the host's working tree therefore changes nothing on a running controller, with one exception: a local `paused: true` is honoured (see the kill switch), and only that key is read locally. A merged change applies on the next tick without a pull. Symlinks and submodules under the role directories are rejected, and a config that cannot be fetched or does not validate counts as paused. If `origin/main` cannot be loaded at startup, `ard serve` starts paused instead of exiting, posts the load error to the status issue once per distinct error, and retries every tick; no loop runs until a config has loaded. `ard config check` validates the working tree, for authoring; `ard config check --ref <ref>` validates a commit of the local checkout (for example `--ref origin/main` after `git fetch`) without fetching.\n \ndiff --git a/internal/initcmd/body.go b/internal/initcmd/body.go\nindex b9fea42..6a5ccd0 100644\n--- a/internal/initcmd/body.go\n+++ b/internal/initcmd/body.go\n@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@ func initBody(ops []op, res *config.Resolved) string {\n \tb.WriteString(\"\\n## Before you merge\\n\\n\")\n \tb.WriteString(\"- Nothing takes effect until this is merged: ard serve reads its configuration from origin/main.\\n\")\n \tb.WriteString(\"- Merge with **Squash and merge** (recommended); **Create a merge commit** is also safe. Never fast-forward this branch into main from the command line: the bot-commit check reads main's first-parent history and would fail on the bot's commit.\\n\")\n+\tb.WriteString(\"- `scanners/trufflehog` is included. It files leaked-credential issues for a human (never for an agent) and needs a TruffleHog binary (AGPL-3.0; it is installed by the role's Dockerfile or taken from the host, and is not in the ard image). To opt out, delete `.ard/scanners/trufflehog/` and its `scanners/trufflehog` line under `overrides:` in `.ard/config.yaml` before merging.\\n\")\n \tb.WriteString(\"\\n## Follow-up the App cannot do\\n\\n\")\n \tb.WriteString(\"ard's GitHub App has no permission to write `.github/`, so do this by hand:\\n\\n\")\n \tb.WriteString(\"1. Copy `.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml` from the ard repository into this repository.\\n\")\ndiff --git a/internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go b/internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go\nindex 6666878..41e2e08 100644\n--- a/internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go\n+++ b/internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go\n@@ -143,7 +143,7 @@ func snapshot(t *testing.T, dir string) map[string]string {\n \treturn m\n }\n \n-var starterTree = []string{\".ard/config.yaml\", \".ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/license-review/allowlist.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/license-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/scanners/cve/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/cve/merge.jq\", \".ard/scanners/cve/scan\", \".ard/scanners/docs/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/docs/docscan.go\", \".ard/scanners/docs/scan\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/scan\", \".ard/triage/architect/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/designer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/documentation-planner/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/product-manager/prompt.txt\", \".ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt\"}\n+var starterTree = []string{\".ard/config.yaml\", \".ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/license-review/allowlist.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/license-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/scanners/cve/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/cve/merge.jq\", \".ard/scanners/cve/scan\", \".ard/scanners/docs/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/docs/docscan.go\", \".ard/scanners/docs/scan\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/scan\", \".ard/scanners/trufflehog/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/trufflehog/exclude-paths\", \".ard/scanners/trufflehog/findings.jq\", \".ard/scanners/trufflehog/scan\", \".ard/triage/architect/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/designer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/documentation-planner/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/product-manager/prompt.txt\", \".ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt\"}\n \n func TestInitOpensPR(t *testing.T) {\n \th := newHarness(t)\n@@ -198,7 +198,7 @@ func TestInitOpensPR(t *testing.T) {\n \tif pr.HeadRef != \"ard-init\" || pr.BaseRef != \"main\" || pr.Draft {\n \t\tt.Errorf(\"pr = %+v\", pr)\n \t}\n-\tfor _, s := range []string{\"bot-commits.yml\", \"ARD_BOT_LOGIN\", \"Squash and merge\", \".ard/scanners/cve/scan\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/scan\", \".ard/triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt\"} {\n+\tfor _, s := range []string{\"bot-commits.yml\", \"ARD_BOT_LOGIN\", \"Squash and merge\", \".ard/scanners/cve/scan\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/scan\", \".ard/scanners/trufflehog/scan\", \"delete `.ard/scanners/trufflehog/`\", \".ard/triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt\"} {\n \t\tif !strings.Contains(pr.Body, s) {\n \t\t\tt.Errorf(\"PR body lacks %q:\\n%s\", s, pr.Body)\n \t\t}\ndiff --git a/internal/roles/config.yaml b/internal/roles/config.yaml\nindex ee5d654..350e907 100644\n--- a/internal/roles/config.yaml\n+++ b/internal/roles/config.yaml\n@@ -30,6 +30,9 @@ overrides:\n   scanners/cve: { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\n   scanners/docs: { every: 3d, max_open: 3, group_size: 10, autoclose: true }\n   scanners/error-codes: { every: 24h, group_size: 20, autoclose: true }\n+  # Leaked credentials go straight to a human: route: needs-human files without\n+  # ard:pending, so no agent triages them.\n+  scanners/trufflehog: { every: 24h, max_open: 5, group_size: 1, autoclose: true, route: needs-human, timeout: 30m }\n   triage/lead:  { model: claude-opus-5-5, timeout: 15m }\n   triage/product-manager: { model: claude-opus-5-5 }\n   triage/architect: { model: claude-opus-5-5, after: [product-manager] }\ndiff --git a/internal/roles/roles.go b/internal/roles/roles.go\nindex 7f70fa4..03baf3c 100644\n--- a/internal/roles/roles.go\n+++ b/internal/roles/roles.go\n@@ -7,11 +7,11 @@ package roles\n import \"embed\"\n \n // FS is the starter .ard/ tree `ard init` proposes: config.yaml plus the role\n-// directories (scanners/cve, scanners/docs, scanners/error-codes, triage/lead, triage/engineer, triage/product-manager, triage/architect, triage/designer, triage/documentation-planner, workers/engineer, reviewers/eng-review, reviewers/license-review and reviewers/security-review); paths are relative to .ard/.\n+// directories (scanners/cve, scanners/docs, scanners/error-codes, scanners/trufflehog, triage/lead, triage/engineer, triage/product-manager, triage/architect, triage/designer, triage/documentation-planner, workers/engineer, reviewers/eng-review, reviewers/license-review and reviewers/security-review); paths are relative to .ard/.\n //\n // scanners/missing-tests is left out until its scan driver exists; re-add it when wiring it in.\n //\n-//go:embed config.yaml reviewers scanners/cve scanners/docs scanners/error-codes triage workers\n+//go:embed config.yaml reviewers scanners/cve scanners/docs scanners/error-codes scanners/trufflehog triage workers\n var FS embed.FS\n \n // ExecutableNames lists base names that must be written 0755.\ndiff --git a/internal/roles/roles_test.go b/internal/roles/roles_test.go\nindex 01234b3..8379b4a 100644\n--- a/internal/roles/roles_test.go\n+++ b/internal/roles/roles_test.go\n@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@ func TestFSContents(t *testing.T) {\n \t\tt.Fatal(err)\n \t}\n \tsort.Strings(got)\n-\twant := []string{\"config.yaml\", \"reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \"reviewers/license-review/allowlist.txt\", \"reviewers/license-review/prompt.txt\", \"reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt\", \"scanners/cve/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/cve/merge.jq\", \"scanners/cve/scan\", \"scanners/docs/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/docs/docscan.go\", \"scanners/docs/scan\", \"scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \"scanners/error-codes/scan\", \"triage/architect/prompt.txt\", \"triage/designer/prompt.txt\", \"triage/documentation-planner/prompt.txt\", \"triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \"triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \"triage/product-manager/prompt.txt\", \"workers/engineer/prompt.txt\"}\n+\twant := []string{\"config.yaml\", \"reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \"reviewers/license-review/allowlist.txt\", \"reviewers/license-review/prompt.txt\", \"reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt\", \"scanners/cve/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/cve/merge.jq\", \"scanners/cve/scan\", \"scanners/docs/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/docs/docscan.go\", \"scanners/docs/scan\", \"scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \"scanners/error-codes/scan\", \"scanners/trufflehog/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/trufflehog/exclude-paths\", \"scanners/trufflehog/findings.jq\", \"scanners/trufflehog/scan\", \"triage/architect/prompt.txt\", \"triage/designer/prompt.txt\", \"triage/documentation-planner/prompt.txt\", \"triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \"triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \"triage/product-manager/prompt.txt\", \"workers/engineer/prompt.txt\"}\n \tif strings.Join(got, \",\") != strings.Join(want, \",\") {\n \t\tt.Fatalf(\"embedded files = %v, want %v\", got, want)\n \t}\n@@ -43,7 +43,7 @@ func TestFSContents(t *testing.T) {\n // embed.FS reports 0444 for everything, so the exec bit must be checked on disk\n // to catch a mode lost in git.\n func TestScanIsExecutableOnDisk(t *testing.T) {\n-\tfor _, p := range []string{\"scanners/cve/scan\", \"scanners/docs/scan\", \"scanners/error-codes/scan\"} {\n+\tfor _, p := range []string{\"scanners/cve/scan\", \"scanners/docs/scan\", \"scanners/error-codes/scan\", \"scanners/trufflehog/scan\"} {\n \t\tfi, err := os.Stat(p)\n \t\tif err != nil {\n \t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n@@ -168,3 +168,29 @@ func starterFS(t *testing.T, chmod bool) fstest.MapFS {\n \t}\n \treturn m\n }\n+\n+func TestEmbeddedTrufflehogRoleLoadsAsScanner(t *testing.T) {\n+\tres, err := config.LoadFS(starterFS(t, true), \"/repo\")\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"LoadFS: %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+\tfor _, r := range res.Roles {\n+\t\tif r.Kind != config.KindScanner || r.Name != \"trufflehog\" {\n+\t\t\tcontinue\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tif r.ScanPath != \".ard/scanners/trufflehog/scan\" || !r.Autoclose || r.Every != 24*time.Hour || r.GroupSize != 1 || r.MaxOpen != 5 || r.Timeout != 30*time.Minute {\n+\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"unexpected role: %+v\", r)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tif r.Route != config.RouteNeedsHuman {\n+\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"Route = %v, want needs-human\", r.Route)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tif r.Dockerfile != \".ard/scanners/trufflehog/Dockerfile\" {\n+\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"Dockerfile = %q\", r.Dockerfile)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tif !slices.Equal(r.Extra, []string{\"exclude-paths\", \"findings.jq\"}) {\n+\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"Extra = %v, want [exclude-paths findings.jq]\", r.Extra)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\treturn\n+\t}\n+\tt.Fatal(\"no scanner role trufflehog\")\n+}\ndiff --git a/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/Dockerfile b/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/Dockerfile\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..3d54fc7\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/Dockerfile\n@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@\n+# Pinned tool image for the trufflehog scanner. Versions verified 2026-11-23:\n+#   trufflehog 3.100.0 (released 2026-11-19), jq 1.8.2.\n+# The trufflehog tarball checksums come from trufflehog_3.100.0_checksums.txt,\n+# whose signature was verified on 2026-11-23 with cosign v3.1.4 (\"Verified OK\"):\n+#   cosign verify-blob trufflehog_3.100.0_checksums.txt \\\n+#     --certificate trufflehog_3.100.0_checksums.txt.pem \\\n+#     --signature trufflehog_3.100.0_checksums.txt.sig \\\n+#     --certificate-identity-regexp 'https://github\\.com/trufflesecurity/trufflehog/' \\\n+#     --certificate-oidc-issuer https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com\n+# jq's checksums are the ones in scanners/cve/Dockerfile.\n+# The base is the same golang:1.27.4-trixie index digest as cve and the ard\n+# image (root Dockerfile), so the layers are shared.\n+#\n+# LICENCE: trufflehog is AGPL-3.0. It is downloaded into this role's image only;\n+# the binary is NOT in the published ard image.\n+#\n+# The image does NOT copy `scan` or `findings.jq`: the executor mounts this role\n+# directory read-only, so the mounted script is always the one that runs.\n+# Run:  docker run --rm -v \"$PWD\":/repo:ro -v <role dir>:/role:ro -w /repo IMAGE /role/scan\n+\n+ARG GO_IMAGE=golang:1.27.4-trixie@sha256:f18c3d73a184fb0582828510722e723b63a93f7188d11dd223d9be6f6880e65d\n+\n+FROM ${GO_IMAGE} AS tools\n+ARG TARGETARCH\n+ARG TRUFFLEHOG_VERSION=3.100.0\n+ARG TRUFFLEHOG_SHA256_AMD64=b2d85eba59865e98f45c9fc9f77d2c6d62df529fdd5755af121304ea5a7cecbb\n+ARG TRUFFLEHOG_SHA256_ARM64=aa61657049229ae523e8455fcbba87dff57b0a2ba6bdb391a38cf75e6d4016dd\n+ARG JQ_VERSION=1.8.2\n+ARG JQ_SHA256_AMD64=b1c22172dd303f3be49e935aa56aa48a8b7a46e0bc838b4997d3bb451495870f\n+ARG JQ_SHA256_ARM64=8b85c817833814ddca00a144c33705546355afccf0cf39b188f3cdb48b852309\n+RUN set -eu; \\\n+    case \"${TARGETARCH}\" in \\\n+      amd64) th_sha=\"${TRUFFLEHOG_SHA256_AMD64}\"; jq_sha=\"${JQ_SHA256_AMD64}\" ;; \\\n+      arm64) th_sha=\"${TRUFFLEHOG_SHA256_ARM64}\"; jq_sha=\"${JQ_SHA256_ARM64}\" ;; \\\n+      *) echo \"unsupported arch: ${TARGETARCH}\" >&2; exit 1 ;; \\\n+    esac; \\\n+    mkdir /out; \\\n+    curl -fsSL -o /tmp/th.tgz \"https://github.com/trufflesecurity/trufflehog/releases/download/v${TRUFFLEHOG_VERSION}/trufflehog_${TRUFFLEHOG_VERSION}_linux_${TARGETARCH}.tar.gz\"; \\\n+    echo \"${th_sha}  /tmp/th.tgz\" | sha256sum -c -; \\\n+    tar -xzf /tmp/th.tgz -C /out trufflehog; \\\n+    curl -fsSL -o /out/jq \"https://github.com/jqlang/jq/releases/download/jq-${JQ_VERSION}/jq-linux-${TARGETARCH}\"; \\\n+    echo \"${jq_sha}  /out/jq\" | sha256sum -c -; \\\n+    chmod 0755 /out/trufflehog /out/jq\n+\n+FROM ${GO_IMAGE}\n+COPY --from=tools /out/trufflehog /usr/local/bin/trufflehog\n+COPY --from=tools /out/jq /usr/local/bin/jq\n+# The executor's /tmp is a noexec tmpfs; keep the temp dir in /var/tmp.\n+ENV TMPDIR=/var/tmp\ndiff --git a/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/exclude-paths b/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/exclude-paths\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..b83ab0b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/exclude-paths\n@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@\n+# trufflehog path regexes (Go RE2), one per line, matched against repo-relative\n+# paths. Human-owned: change it in a reviewed PR. scan drops # lines and blanks.\n+# .ard/<n>/logs/ were secret-scanned at close-out (model signature blobs are noise).\n+^\\.ard/[0-9]+/logs/\n+^vendor/\n+^node_modules/\ndiff --git a/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/findings.jq b/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/findings.jq\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..23ef8a6\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/findings.jq\n@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@\n+# project: trufflehog --json result lines in; one \"<base64 secret>\\t<json>\" line out\n+#          per result. The json holds only d (DetectorName), f (file), l (line).\n+#          Errors carry fixed text only (scan drops this stage's stderr anyway).\n+# merge:   \"<h16>\\t<json>\" lines in (-n -R, inputs); findings out.\n+def die(m): error(\"trufflehog: \" + m);\n+\n+def project:\n+  if type != \"object\" then die(\"result is not an object\") else . end\n+  | (.SourceMetadata.Data.Filesystem // die(\"result has no filesystem location\")) as $fs\n+  | (if (.Raw | type) == \"string\" and .Raw != \"\" then .Raw\n+     elif (.RawV2 | type) == \"string\" and .RawV2 != \"\" then .RawV2\n+     else die(\"result has no Raw or RawV2 value\") end) as $secret\n+  | (.DetectorName | if type == \"string\" and test(\"^[A-Za-z0-9_.-]{1,64}$\") then . else die(\"bad detector name\") end) as $d\n+  | ($fs.file | if type == \"string\" then ltrimstr(\"./\") else die(\"result file is not a string\") end) as $f\n+  | if $f == \"\" or ($f | startswith(\"/\")) or ($f | split(\"/\") | any(. == \"..\" or . == \".\" or . == \"\"))\n+       or ($f | explode | any(. < 32 or . == 127))\n+    then die(\"result file is not a clean repo-relative path\") else . end\n+  | ($fs.line // 0 | if type == \"number\" and . >= 0 then floor else die(\"bad line\") end) as $l\n+  | \"\\($secret | @base64)\\t\\({d: $d, f: $f, l: $l} | tojson)\";\n+\n+# A code span whose fence is longer than any backtick run in the text.\n+def code: ([match(\"`+\"; \"g\").length] | max // 0) as $n | (\"`\" * ($n + 1)) as $fence\n+  | if $n > 0 then \"\\($fence) \\(.) \\($fence)\" else \"\\($fence)\\(.)\\($fence)\" end;\n+\n+def merge($allow):\n+  [inputs | select(length > 0) | split(\"\\t\")\n+   | if length != 2 or (.[0] | test(\"^[0-9a-f]{16}$\") | not) then die(\"bad hashed line\") else . end\n+   | {h: .[0]} + (.[1] | fromjson)]\n+  | map(select((\"trufflehog:\" + .h) as $fp | $allow | index($fp) | not))\n+  | group_by(.h)\n+  | map((\"trufflehog:\" + .[0].h) as $fp\n+      | (map(.d) | unique) as $dets\n+      | (map({f, l}) | unique_by([.f, .l]) | sort_by(.f, .l)) as $locs\n+      | ($locs | map(.f) | unique) as $files\n+      | {fingerprint: $fp,\n+         title: (\"Possible \\($dets[0]) credential in \\($files[0])\" | .[0:200]),\n+         severity: \"high\", group: \"\", files: $files[0:1000],\n+         body: ([\n+           \"trufflehog matched a value that looks like a credential (detector: \\($dets | map(code) | join(\", \"))). ard did not verify it and never stores or prints the value.\",\n+           \"\",\n+           \"**Treat it as leaked.** Revoke or rotate it at the provider first. Deleting the line does not revoke it: the value stays in git history, and on a public repository it is already public.\",\n+           \"\",\n+           \"**Do not add `ard:pending` to this issue before the credential is rotated.** Triage and worker agents would read the file that holds it.\",\n+           \"\",\n+           \"What to do: 1. Rotate or revoke the credential at the provider. 2. Remove the value from HEAD in a PR. The issue closes itself on the next run (within 24 hours) once the value is gone from HEAD; that means gone from HEAD, not rotated. 3. Do not close this issue as completed while the value is still at HEAD: the next run refiles it. 4. For a false positive or a test fixture, add the fingerprint to `allow` or the path to `exclude-paths` (a reviewed PR), or close as not planned (it refiles after 90 days). 5. At 5 open issues the scanner does not run, so close fixed ones by hand once the value is gone. 6. Git history is not scanned or rewritten; rotation is what makes that safe.\",\n+           \"\",\n+           \"Not a secret? A maintainer adds the fingerprint below to `.ard/scanners/trufflehog/allow`, or a path pattern to `.ard/scanners/trufflehog/exclude-paths`, in a reviewed PR. Inline `trufflehog:ignore` comments are not honoured.\",\n+           \"\",\n+           \"Fingerprint: `\\($fp)`\",\n+           \"\",\n+           \"Locations at the scanned commit (\\($locs | length)):\"]\n+           + ($locs[0:50] | map(\"- \\(.f | code)\" + (if .l > 0 then \" line \\(.l)\" else \"\" end)))\n+        